OL,3,CProgramme listings for SUN 31 MAY
OL,4,G1945FWords and Music
OL,5,     GWords about Marilyn Monroe, Helen
OL,6,     Gof Troy and a host of other
OL,7,     Gbeauties both real and imagined
OL,8,     Gby Sappho, Austen, Oscar Wilde.
OL,9,     GAnd music to match from
OL,10,     GTchaikovsky, Bach, Judith Weir.
OL,11,G2100FUltimate Calm with Erland Cooper
OL,12,     GErland Cooper finds calm in the
OL,13,     Gstillness with a selection of
OL,14,     Gpieces inspired by solitude while
OL,15,     Gharpist Mary Lattimore shares her
OL,16,     Gsafe haven.
OL,17,G2200FNight Tracks
OL,18,     GSara Mohr-Pietsch presents an
OL,19,     Gadventurous, immersive soundtrack
OL,20,     Gfor late-night listening, from
OL,21,     Gclassical to contemporary and
OL,22,     Geverything in between.
OL,23,Vppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
